## Practical Information

CO₂ therapy is available at all Ensana Spa Hotels in Marienbad. A single treatment lasts 20-30 minutes and is typically administered once daily over a period of 7-21 days. Optimal results develop with a minimum course of 14 days.

Before beginning treatment, a medical examination determines your individual therapy plan. Contraindications include acute inflammation, uncontrolled heart failure and certain skin conditions.

## Frequently Asked Questions about CO₂ Therapy

### What is "Maria's gas"?

Maria's gas is natural carbon dioxide of 99.7% purity rising from the volcanic subsoil of the Slavkovský les (Kaiserwald) forest. It is one of Marienbad's four natural healing resources and has been used therapeutically in a systematic way for over 150 years.

### What happens during a dry CO₂ gas bath — does it hurt?

You lie for 20 to 30 minutes in a special bag reaching up to your neck, which is filled with natural CO₂. The treatment is completely painless; most guests feel only a pleasant sensation of warmth and gentle tingling as the gas is absorbed through the skin and dilates the blood vessels.

### Which conditions does CO₂ therapy help with?

It is used above all for high blood pressure and peripheral circulation disorders, for musculoskeletal conditions such as osteoarthritis, for impaired wound healing and diabetic polyneuropathy, as well as in rehabilitation and for exhaustion syndromes.

### How many treatments are needed before I feel an effect?

Treatment usually takes place once a day over 7 to 21 days; the optimal effect unfolds with a cure lasting at least 14 days. After a two-week cure, a reduction of systolic blood pressure by up to 10–15 mmHg has been documented.

### Are there contraindications?

Yes. CO₂ therapy is not applied in cases of acute inflammation, uncontrolled heart failure and certain skin diseases. Every cure therefore begins with a medical examination, during which your individual treatment plan is drawn up.

### Where can I book CO₂ therapy?

CO₂ therapy is available in all Ensana spa hotels in Marienbad. The most comprehensive programme — dry gas baths, carbonic baths and gas injections — is offered by the five-star Ensana Nové Lázně.
